# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DO NOT COMMIT THE REAL .env FILE.
#
# This .env.example is a template and is safe to commit (no real values).
# The real .env is already gitignored at the repo root — keep it that way.
#
# Every variable below is a credential. Treat them like passwords:
#   CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN — grants access to your Claude.ai subscription.
#   GITHUB_TOKEN            — grants push/read access to the GitHub repo you
#                             scoped it to (only set if you want Claude to
#                             push directly; see README "Pushing your work
#                             to a remote", Option B).
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Optional. Only needed for headless mode (`claude -p "..."`).
#
# To generate a token, run `setup-token` inside an interactive session:
#   ./claude.sh run example -- setup-token
# Follow the prompts, then paste the result here.
#
# For normal interactive use you don't need this file at all — the OAuth login
# from `/login` is persisted to ./claude_home/ and reused automatically.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# Optional. Only needed if you want Claude to `git push` directly from inside
# the container. Leave it unset to use the recommended host-side push flow
# (commit inside the container, push from a host terminal — no credentials
# enter the container). See "Pushing your work to a remote" in README.md.
#
# If you set this, use a GitHub fine-grained personal access token scoped to
# the single repo you're working on, with the minimum permissions needed
# (`Contents: Read & write` is enough for `git push`). Set a short expiry
# (30–90 days) so a leak self-heals.
#GITHUB_TOKEN=
